IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc3-periods`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-payments`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 5 (housing costs element for owner-occupiers).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- WHAT IS LEFT OF THIS SCHEDULE. Paragraphs 10, 11 and 12 (interest on loans, alternative finance, the standard rate) and paragraph 3(2) show only
-- dots in this text, and Schedule 1 paragraphs 4 to 6 (owner-occupier payments, loan interest payments, alternative finance payments) too, so
-- the only relevant payments left are service charge payments (paragraph 3(1)). The element is the monthly total of the service charge payments
-- taken into account (paragraph 13), once the earned-income exception (paragraph 4) and the qualifying period (paragraph 5) are out of the way.
--
-- OUT OF RANGE, taken as facts: regulation 26(3) (who is an owner-occupier) and 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership), regulation 25(5) (the payment,
-- liability and occupation conditions), and earned income (Chapter 2 of Part 6, piece uc2).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 1: who is an owner-occupier.
-- src:2608 | (1) This Schedule contains provisions about claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies.
-- src:2609 | (2) Claimants who fall within sub-paragraph (1) are referred to in this Schedule as “owner-occupiers” (and references to “joint owner-occupiers” are to joint claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies).
@ref Sch 5 para 1(1) and (2) (src:2608-2609)
DECLARE `Claimant who may be an owner-occupier` HAS
    -- out of range: reg 26(3) (piece uc1)
    `regulation 26(3) applies to the claimant`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim basis`                                         IS A `Claim basis`

-- src:2608 | (1) This Schedule contains provisions about claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies.
-- src:2609 | (2) Claimants who fall within sub-paragraph (1) are referred to in this Schedule as “owner-occupiers” (and references to “joint owner-occupiers” are to joint claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies).
@ref Sch 5 para 1(1) and (2) (src:2608-2609)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant who may be an owner-occupier`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 1(2) — a claimant is an owner-occupier` claimant MEANS
    claimant's `regulation 26(3) applies to the claimant`

-- src:2609 | (2) Claimants who fall within sub-paragraph (1) are referred to in this Schedule as “owner-occupiers” (and references to “joint owner-occupiers” are to joint claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies).
@ref Sch 5 para 1(2) "joint owner-occupiers" (src:2609)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant who may be an owner-occupier`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 1(2) — a joint owner-occupier` claimant MEANS
    (claimant's `regulation 26(3) applies to the claimant`)
    AND ((claimant's `claim basis`) EQUALS `joint claimants`)

-- Paragraph 2, "relevant date": the date on which an amount calculated under this Schedule is first included in the owner-occupier's award.
-- The text defines it and never uses it again in this range; the rule gives the definition a home.
-- src:2621 | “relevant date” means, in relation to an owner-occupier, the date on which an amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule is first included in the owner-occupier’s award;
@ref Sch 5 para 2 "relevant date" (src:2621)
GIVEN `date on which an amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule is first included in the owner-occupier's award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 5 para 2 — the relevant date` `date on which an amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule is first included in the owner-occupier's award` MEANS
    `date on which an amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule is first included in the owner-occupier's award`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 3: the relevant payments are the service charge payments, as paragraphs 7 and 8 of Schedule 1 (the dangling "that Schedule" of
-- sub-paragraph (3), read as Schedule 1: fork U3-F2) understand them. Schedule 1 paragraph 8(1)(b) makes the additional conditions apply to a
-- Schedule 5 calculation, so a payment record for this Schedule has the field `the calculation is made under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5` true.
-- src:2625 | (1) “Relevant payments” means one or more payments which are service charge payments.
-- src:2626 | (2) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:2627 | (3) “Service charge payments” is to be understood in accordance with paragraphs 7 and 8 of that Schedule.
@ref Sch 5 para 3 (src:2625-2627)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment that may be a service charge payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 3 — the payment is a relevant payment` payment MEANS
    (`Sch 1 para 7(1) — a service charge payment` payment)
    AND ((payment's `facts for paragraph 8`)'s `the calculation is made under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 4: no housing costs element for an assessment period in which the owner-occupier, or either member of a couple, has any earned income.
-- Whether income is earned income is Chapter 2 of Part 6 (piece uc2): a stated input.
-- src:2630 | (1) Section 11(1) of the Act (housing costs) does not apply to any owner-occupier in relation to an assessment period where—
-- src:2631 | (a) the owner-occupier has any earned income; or
-- src:2632 | (b) if the owner-occupier is a member of a couple, either member of the couple has any earned income.
-- src:2633 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) applies irrespective of the nature of the work engaged in, its duration or the amount of the earned income.
-- src:2634 | (3) Nothing in this paragraph prevents an amount calculated under Schedule 4 from being included in the award of any claimant who falls within regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership).
@ref Sch 5 para 4 (src:2630-2634)
DECLARE `Owner-occupier's earned income in an assessment period` HAS
    `claim basis`                                                                  IS A `Claim basis`
    -- out of range: Chapter 2 of Part 6, earned income (piece uc2)
    `the owner-occupier has any earned income`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other member of the couple has any earned income`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- sub-paragraph (2): the nature of the work, its duration and the amount of the earned income are irrelevant; no rule reads them
    `the nature of the work engaged in`                                            IS A STRING
    `the duration of the work`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the amount of the earned income`                                              IS A NUMBER

-- src:2630 | (1) Section 11(1) of the Act (housing costs) does not apply to any owner-occupier in relation to an assessment period where—
-- src:2631 | (a) the owner-occupier has any earned income; or
-- src:2632 | (b) if the owner-occupier is a member of a couple, either member of the couple has any earned income.
-- src:2633 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) applies irrespective of the nature of the work engaged in, its duration or the amount of the earned income.
@ref Sch 5 para 4(1) and (2) (src:2630-2633)
GIVEN earnings IS A `Owner-occupier's earned income in an assessment period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 4 — section 11(1) of the Act does not apply to the owner-occupier for the assessment period` earnings MEANS
    (earnings's `the owner-occupier has any earned income`)
    OR (    (`reg 2 — the claimant has a partner` (earnings's `claim basis`))
        AND (earnings's `the other member of the couple has any earned income`))

-- src:2634 | (3) Nothing in this paragraph prevents an amount calculated under Schedule 4 from being included in the award of any claimant who falls within regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership).
@ref Sch 5 para 4(3) (src:2634)
GIVEN `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 4(3) — paragraph 4 does not prevent an amount calculated under Schedule 4 from being included` `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies` MEANS
    `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 5: the qualifying period of 9 consecutive assessment periods. The assessment periods are given oldest first, ending with the one in question.
-- A new award: each period counts when the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit and would otherwise qualify; after an amount has ceased
-- to be included: each period counts when the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify. A period that does not count stops the period running (5(3)(a));
-- a new one starts only when the requirements are met again (5(3)(b)), which restarts the count at nil.
-- Paragraph 6(2) and paragraph 7(2) start the count above nil (credited and carried-forward periods).
-- src:2638 | (2) “Qualifying period” means a period of—
-- src:2639 | (a) in the case of a new award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which——
-- src:2640 | (i) the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit, and
-- src:2641 | (ii) would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award;
-- src:2642 | (b) in any case where an amount calculated under this Schedule has for any reason ceased to be included in the award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award.
-- src:2643 | (3) Where, before the end of a qualifying period, an owner-occupier for any reason ceases to qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule—
-- src:2644 | (a) that qualifying period stops running; and
-- src:2645 | (b) a new qualifying period starts only when the owner-occupier again meets the requirements of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b).
@ref Sch 5 para 5(2) and (3) (src:2638-2645)
DECLARE `Kind of qualifying period` IS ONE OF
    `a new award`
    `an award from which an amount calculated under this Schedule has ceased to be included`

-- src:2638 | (2) “Qualifying period” means a period of—
-- src:2639 | (a) in the case of a new award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which——
-- src:2640 | (i) the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit, and
-- src:2641 | (ii) would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award;
-- src:2642 | (b) in any case where an amount calculated under this Schedule has for any reason ceased to be included in the award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award.
@ref Sch 5 para 5(2) (src:2638-2642)
DECLARE `Assessment period for the qualifying period` HAS
    `the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit in the assessment period`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2638 | (2) “Qualifying period” means a period of—
-- src:2639 | (a) in the case of a new award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which——
-- src:2640 | (i) the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit, and
-- src:2641 | (ii) would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award;
-- src:2642 | (b) in any case where an amount calculated under this Schedule has for any reason ceased to be included in the award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award.
@ref Sch 5 para 5(2) (src:2638-2642)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of qualifying period`
      period IS A `Assessment period for the qualifying period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 5(2) — the assessment period counts towards the qualifying period` kind period MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a new award` THEN (period's `the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit in the assessment period`) AND (period's `the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award`)
    WHEN `an award from which an amount calculated under this Schedule has ceased to be included` THEN period's `the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award`

-- Walks the periods from oldest to newest. `run` is the number of consecutive qualifying periods so far (it may start above nil); `ended` is whether
-- a run of 9 has been completed in an earlier period. At the last period the answer is `ended` as it stood BEFORE that period is looked at:
-- the qualifying period must have ended in an EARLIER assessment period for the element to be included from this one (paragraph 5(1)).
-- src:2637 | (1) An owner-occupier's award of universal credit is not to include any amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule until the beginning of the assessment period that follows the assessment period in which the qualifying period ends.
@ref Sch 5 para 5(1) (src:2637)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of qualifying period`
      periods IS A LIST OF `Assessment period for the qualifying period`
      run IS A NUMBER
      ended IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 5(1) — the qualifying period ended in an earlier assessment period` kind periods run ended MEANS
    CONSIDER periods
    WHEN EMPTY THEN ended
    WHEN period FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF null rest
        THEN ended
        ELSE `Sch 5 para 5(1) — the qualifying period ended in an earlier assessment period` kind rest
                 (IF `Sch 5 para 5(2) — the assessment period counts towards the qualifying period` kind period THEN run PLUS 1 ELSE 0)
                 (ended OR ((IF `Sch 5 para 5(2) — the assessment period counts towards the qualifying period` kind period THEN run PLUS 1 ELSE 0) AT LEAST 9))

-- src:2636 | 5 No housing costs element under this Schedule for qualifying period
-- src:2637 | (1) An owner-occupier's award of universal credit is not to include any amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule until the beginning of the assessment period that follows the assessment period in which the qualifying period ends.
-- src:2638 | (2) “Qualifying period” means a period of—
-- src:2639 | (a) in the case of a new award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which——
-- src:2640 | (i) the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit, and
-- src:2641 | (ii) would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award;
-- src:2642 | (b) in any case where an amount calculated under this Schedule has for any reason ceased to be included in the award, 9 consecutive assessment periods in relation to which the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award.
-- src:2643 | (3) Where, before the end of a qualifying period, an owner-occupier for any reason ceases to qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule—
-- src:2644 | (a) that qualifying period stops running; and
-- src:2645 | (b) a new qualifying period starts only when the owner-occupier again meets the requirements of sub-paragraph (2)(a) or (b).
@ref Sch 5 para 5 (src:2636-2645)
DECLARE `Facts about the qualifying period` HAS
    `kind of qualifying period`                                                                            IS A `Kind of qualifying period`
    `assessment periods, oldest first, ending with the one in question`                                   IS A LIST OF `Assessment period for the qualifying period`
    `assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2)`           IS A NUMBER
    `paragraph 7(3) applies: an amount calculated under this Schedule was already included in the award that ended`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Paragraph 7(3): where an amount was already included in the terminated award, no qualifying period applies to the further award.
-- src:2657 | (3) But where, immediately before the joint owner-occupiers' award was terminated, an amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule was already included in the award, no qualifying period under paragraph 5 applies to the owner-occupier in relation to the commencement of the further award (or each further award).
@ref Sch 5 para 7(3) (src:2657)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the qualifying period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 5 — the owner-occupier is past the qualifying period` facts MEANS
    (facts's `paragraph 7(3) applies: an amount calculated under this Schedule was already included in the award that ended`)
    OR (`Sch 5 para 5(1) — the qualifying period ended in an earlier assessment period` (facts's `kind of qualifying period`) (facts's `assessment periods, oldest first, ending with the one in question`) (facts's `assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2)`) ((facts's `assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2)`) AT LEAST 9))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 6: an owner-occupier entitled to JSA or ESA immediately before the award. Days on which they received it MAY be treated as if they were
-- the whole or part of one or more assessment periods, as the number of days decides. The permission is a stated input; the count is days divided by the
-- days in an assessment period (fork U3-F25: a part of a period is a fraction, and 9 consecutive periods are 9 in all).
-- src:2647 | (1) This paragraph applies to any owner-occupier who immediately before the commencement of an award of universal credit is entitled to—
-- src:2648 | (a) a jobseeker's allowance; or
-- src:2649 | (b) an employment and support allowance.
-- src:2650 | (2) In determining when the qualifying period in paragraph 5 ends in relation to the owner-occupier, any period that comprises only days on which the owner-occupier was receiving a benefit referred to in sub-paragraph (1) may be treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods, as determined by the number of days on which any such benefit was received.
@ref Sch 5 para 6 (src:2647-2650)
DECLARE `Owner-occupier entitled to a jobseeker's allowance or an employment and support allowance` HAS
    `immediately before the commencement of the award of universal credit the owner-occupier is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately before the commencement of the award of universal credit the owner-occupier is entitled to an employment and support allowance`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of days on which the owner-occupier was receiving that benefit in the period`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `the period comprises only days on which the owner-occupier was receiving that benefit`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assessment period used for the count`                                                                                           IS A `Assessment period`

-- src:2647 | (1) This paragraph applies to any owner-occupier who immediately before the commencement of an award of universal credit is entitled to—
-- src:2648 | (a) a jobseeker's allowance; or
-- src:2649 | (b) an employment and support allowance.
-- src:2650 | (2) In determining when the qualifying period in paragraph 5 ends in relation to the owner-occupier, any period that comprises only days on which the owner-occupier was receiving a benefit referred to in sub-paragraph (1) may be treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods, as determined by the number of days on which any such benefit was received.
@ref Sch 5 para 6 (src:2647-2650)
GIVEN owner IS A `Owner-occupier entitled to a jobseeker's allowance or an employment and support allowance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 5 para 6(2) — the assessment periods that the days of benefit are treated as` owner MEANS
    IF (    ((owner's `immediately before the commencement of the award of universal credit the owner-occupier is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`) OR (owner's `immediately before the commencement of the award of universal credit the owner-occupier is entitled to an employment and support allowance`))
        AND (owner's `the period comprises only days on which the owner-occupier was receiving that benefit`)
        AND (owner's `the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods`))
    THEN (owner's `number of days on which the owner-occupier was receiving that benefit in the period`) DIVIDED BY (`core — the number of days in an assessment period` (owner's `the assessment period used for the count`))
    ELSE 0

-- Paragraph 7(1) and (2): joint owner-occupiers whose award ends because they cease to be a couple, and a further award to one or each of them.
-- The whole or part of any assessment period that would have counted under the terminated award is carried forward.
-- src:2652 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2653 | (a) an award of universal credit to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple; and
-- src:2654 | (b) a further award is made to one of them (or to each of them); and
-- src:2655 | (c) in relation to the further award (or in relation to each further award), the occupation condition is met in respect of the same accommodation as that occupied by the joint owner-occupiers as their home.
-- src:2656 | (2) In determining when the qualifying period in paragraph 5 ends in relation to the further award (or each further award), the whole or part of any assessment period which would have counted in relation to the award that is terminated is to be carried forward and taken into account in relation to the further award (or each further award).
-- src:2657 | (3) But where, immediately before the joint owner-occupiers' award was terminated, an amount of housing costs element calculated under this Schedule was already included in the award, no qualifying period under paragraph 5 applies to the owner-occupier in relation to the commencement of the further award (or each further award).
-- src:2658 | (4) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1)(b), it is irrelevant whether the further award—
-- src:2659 | (a) is made on a claim; or
-- src:2660 | (b) by virtue of regulation 9(6) of the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Claims and Payments) Regulations 2013 is made without a claim.
@ref Sch 5 para 7(1), (2) and (4) (src:2652-2656) (src:2658-2660)
DECLARE `Further award after joint owner-occupiers cease to be a couple` HAS
    `an award of universal credit to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a further award is made to one of them (or to each of them)`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1), the occupation condition
    `in relation to the further award the occupation condition is met in respect of the same accommodation as that occupied by the joint owner-occupiers as their home`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `assessment periods which would have counted in relation to the award that is terminated`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `the further award is made on a claim`                                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2652 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2653 | (a) an award of universal credit to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple; and
-- src:2654 | (b) a further award is made to one of them (or to each of them); and
-- src:2655 | (c) in relation to the further award (or in relation to each further award), the occupation condition is met in respect of the same accommodation as that occupied by the joint owner-occupiers as their home.
@ref Sch 5 para 7(1) (src:2652-2655)
GIVEN couple IS A `Further award after joint owner-occupiers cease to be a couple`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 7(1) — this paragraph applies` couple MEANS
    (couple's `an award of universal credit to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple`)
    AND (couple's `a further award is made to one of them (or to each of them)`)
    AND (couple's `in relation to the further award the occupation condition is met in respect of the same accommodation as that occupied by the joint owner-occupiers as their home`)

-- src:2656 | (2) In determining when the qualifying period in paragraph 5 ends in relation to the further award (or each further award), the whole or part of any assessment period which would have counted in relation to the award that is terminated is to be carried forward and taken into account in relation to the further award (or each further award).
@ref Sch 5 para 7(2) (src:2656)
GIVEN couple IS A `Further award after joint owner-occupiers cease to be a couple`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 5 para 7(2) — the assessment periods carried forward to the further award` couple MEANS
    IF `Sch 5 para 7(1) — this paragraph applies` couple
    THEN couple's `assessment periods which would have counted in relation to the award that is terminated`
    ELSE 0

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 8: a relevant payment is taken into account where the owner-occupier meets the payment, liability and occupation conditions in respect
-- of it and the qualifying period has ended; an amount that does not meet the conditions is not taken into account; no payment is counted twice.
-- Service charge free periods (paragraph 13(5)) and the monthly equivalent (13(3), (4)) are decided here, with the payment.
-- src:2662 | 8 Payments to be taken into account
-- src:2663 | (1) Where an owner-occupier meets the payment condition, liability condition and occupation condition in respect of one or more relevant payments and the qualifying period has ended, each of the relevant payments is to be taken into account for the purposes of the calculation under this Part.
-- src:2664 | (2) No account is to be taken of any amount of a relevant payment to the extent that the conditions referred to in sub-paragraph (1) are not met in respect of that amount.
-- src:2665 | (3) Any particular payment for which an owner-occupier is liable is not to be brought into account more than once, whether in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier (but this does not prevent different payments of the same description being brought into account in respect of an assessment period).
@ref Sch 5 para 8 (src:2662-2665)
DECLARE `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment` HAS
    payment                                                                                                      IS A `Payment that may be a service charge payment`
    `amount of each payment in pounds`                                                                           IS A NUMBER
    `how often the payment falls due`                                                                            IS A `Payment interval`
    -- out of range: reg 25(5) (piece uc1)
    `the owner-occupier meets the payment condition in respect of the relevant payment`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner-occupier meets the liability condition in respect of the relevant payment`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner-occupier meets the occupation condition in respect of the relevant payment`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the qualifying period has ended`                                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the arrangements provide for one or more service charge free periods`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `total number of the service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period`  IS A NUMBER

-- src:2663 | (1) Where an owner-occupier meets the payment condition, liability condition and occupation condition in respect of one or more relevant payments and the qualifying period has ended, each of the relevant payments is to be taken into account for the purposes of the calculation under this Part.
-- src:2664 | (2) No account is to be taken of any amount of a relevant payment to the extent that the conditions referred to in sub-paragraph (1) are not met in respect of that amount.
-- src:2665 | (3) Any particular payment for which an owner-occupier is liable is not to be brought into account more than once, whether in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier (but this does not prevent different payments of the same description being brought into account in respect of an assessment period).
@ref Sch 5 para 8 (src:2663-2665)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 8 — the payment is taken into account` liability MEANS
    (`Sch 5 para 3 — the payment is a relevant payment` (liability's payment))
    AND (liability's `the owner-occupier meets the payment condition in respect of the relevant payment`)
    AND (liability's `the owner-occupier meets the liability condition in respect of the relevant payment`)
    AND (liability's `the owner-occupier meets the occupation condition in respect of the relevant payment`)
    AND (liability's `the qualifying period has ended`)
    AND (NOT (liability's `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier`))

-- Paragraph 13(2) to (4): the monthly equivalent, with the number of payments in 12 months a stated input where there are service charge free periods
-- (the 13(4A) formulas are missing from this text: fork U3-F1).
-- src:2680 | Determine the period in respect of which each service charge payment is payable and determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month (see sub-paragraphs (3) and (4)).
-- src:2681 | Step 3
-- src:2682 | If there is more than one service charge payment, add together the amounts determined in step 2. The result is the amount to be included under this Schedule in respect of service charge payments.
-- src:2683 | (3) Where the period in respect of which an owner-occupier is liable to make a service charge payment is not a month, an amount is to be calculated as the monthly equivalent, so for example—
-- src:2684 | (a) weekly payments are multiplied by 52 and divided by 12;
-- src:2685 | (aa) two-weekly payments are multiplied by 26 and divided by 12;
-- src:2686 | (b) four-weekly payments are multiplied by 13 and divided by 12;
-- src:2687 | (c) three-monthly payments are multiplied by 4 and divided by 12; and
-- src:2688 | (d) annual payments are divided by 12.
-- src:2689 | (4) Where an owner-occupier is liable for service charge payments under arrangements that provide for one or more service charge free periods, subject to sub-paragraph (4A), the monthly equivalent is to be calculated over 12 months by reference to the total number of service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period.
@ref Sch 5 para 13(2) to (4) (src:2680) (src:2683-2689)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 5 para 13 — the monthly amount of a service charge payment` liability MEANS
    IF liability's `the arrangements provide for one or more service charge free periods`
    THEN ((liability's `amount of each payment in pounds`) TIMES (liability's `total number of the service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period`)) DIVIDED BY 12
    ELSE `core — the monthly equivalent of a payment` (liability's `amount of each payment in pounds`) (liability's `how often the payment falls due`)

-- src:2674 | 13 Amount in respect of service charge payments
-- src:2675 | (1) This paragraph provides for the calculation of the amount to be included in the owner-occupier's housing costs element under this Schedule in respect of relevant payments which are service charge payments.
-- src:2676 | (2) The amount in respect of the service charge payments is to be calculated as follows.
-- src:2677 | Step 1
-- src:2678 | Determine the amount of each service charge payment.
-- src:2679 | Step 2
-- src:2680 | Determine the period in respect of which each service charge payment is payable and determine the amount of the payment in respect of a month (see sub-paragraphs (3) and (4)).
-- src:2681 | Step 3
-- src:2682 | If there is more than one service charge payment, add together the amounts determined in step 2. The result is the amount to be included under this Schedule in respect of service charge payments.
@ref Sch 5 para 13 (src:2674-2682)
GIVEN liabilities IS A LIST OF `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 5 para 13 — the amount in respect of service charge payments` liabilities MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN liability YIELD IF `Sch 5 para 8 — the payment is taken into account` liability THEN `Sch 5 para 13 — the monthly amount of a service charge payment` liability ELSE 0) liabilities)

-- Paragraph 9: the element is the paragraph 13 amount for the relevant payments taken into account under paragraph 8.
-- src:2667 | The amount of the owner-occupier's housing costs element under this Schedule is the amount resulting from paragraph 13 in respect of all relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 8.
@ref Sch 5 para 9 (src:2667)
GIVEN liabilities IS A LIST OF `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 5 para 9 — the amount of the owner-occupier's housing costs element` liabilities MEANS
    `Sch 5 para 13 — the amount in respect of service charge payments` liabilities

-- Paragraph 13(5): a service charge free period is a period in respect of which the owner-occupier has no liability to make one or more of the service
-- charge payments taken into account under paragraph 8.
-- src:2695 | (5) “Service charge free period” means any period in respect of which the owner-occupier has no liability to make one or more of the service charge payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 8.
@ref Sch 5 para 13(5) (src:2695)
DECLARE `Period of the arrangements for service charge payments` HAS
    `the owner-occupier has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the service charge payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 8`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2695 | (5) “Service charge free period” means any period in respect of which the owner-occupier has no liability to make one or more of the service charge payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 8.
@ref Sch 5 para 13(5) (src:2695)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of the arrangements for service charge payments`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 5 para 13(5) — a service charge free period` period MEANS
    period's `the owner-occupier has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the service charge payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 8`
